      {
        "id": 132771,
        "name": "Spiff",
        "username": "Spiff",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-21T04:54:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>To be completely honest, I think the painted minis are barely acceptable, but they're acceptable. &nbsp;They're not as good as I could have done myself if I still had 25-year-old-me's free time and focus, but they're far better than I actually <em>would</em> have done in the real world, so that makes them a win in my book. &nbsp;I haven't had a chance to play a game with them yet, but I think they should be a step up from using my 3D standups, so I'm satisfied with the purchase.</p><p>For some reason, the person who painted my Ambuscade did a really good job on that one. &nbsp;Whoever you are, Mystery Painter Person, thank you for that.</p><p>I haven't heard much in the way of feedback from people who have bought the painted minis. &nbsp;Anyone else have an opinion from hands-on experience with the painted minis?</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:18.780Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
